  "idea": "Raycast vs Alfred: which Mac productivity launcher takes the crown",
  "text": "A keyboard launcher can easily save you one hundred mouse clicks every single hour. Reaching for your trackpad to switch apps, resize windows, and copy links destroys deep focus. These micro-delays waste thirty minutes of fragmented attention across an average creative or coding workday. Raycast combines clipboard history, window tiling, quick calculations, and app launching under one universal hotkey. You navigate your computer at pure thought speed.",
